    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now let me check the working directory and compile script.The test verifies that `withinRange(char[]...)` throws `IllegalArgumentException` when a pair doesn't have exactly 2 elements. Let me write a clearer version of this test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version adds a descriptive method name (`test14_withinRange_throwsWhenPairLengthIsNotTwo`) and a Javadoc comment explaining the intent — that `withinRange` requires each inner array to be a 2-element `[min, max]` pair, so passing a 6-element array must throw `IllegalArgumentException`."
    }
